#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/README.rst:2
msgid "README"
msgstr "README"

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:1
msgid "triorb_sick_plc_wrapper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:3
msgid ""
"ROS 2 node that bridges TriOrb velocity commands to a SICK FlexiSoft PLC. "
"The node translates `/drive/std_vector2` values into PLC assembly bytes, "
"mirrors PLC feedback bits, and exposes services for emergency stop, PLC/SLS "
"enabling, and watchdog handling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:5
msgid ""
"All topics are prefixed with `ROS_PREFIX` (if set) through the "
"`GET_TOPIC_NAME()` helper so the node can be namespaced without remapping "
"each interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:7
msgid "Repository layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:8
msgid ""
"`include/sick_plc_wrapper.hpp` – Node declaration, PLC bitfield definitions,"
" and helpers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:9
msgid ""
"`src/sick_plc_wrapper.cpp` – Implementation of the bridge, scaling logic, "
"and services."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:10
msgid "`src/ct.cpp`, `src/sha256.cpp` – License verification helpers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:11
msgid ""
"`launch/plc_wrapper.launch.xml` – Example parameterization for FlexiSoft "
"assemblies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:13
msgid "Key features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:14
msgid ""
"Bidirectional byte-array interface to SICK FlexiSoft PLC assemblies with "
"configurable offsets per field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:15
msgid ""
"Scaling of TriOrb drive vectors into PLC-friendly integer representations "
"(direction 0.1°, speed cm/s, rotate °/s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:16
msgid ""
"Watchdog timer that toggles a Jetson → PLC bit while mirroring PLC watchdog "
"responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:17
msgid ""
"Exception-handler publishers for registration, warnings, and errors so "
"operators see PLC issues in a unified feed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:18
msgid ""
"Runtime services to request emergency-stop, PLC deactivate, and SLS disable "
"without touching the PLC UI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:19
msgid ""
"Startup guard that waits (up to 10 s) for both PLC topics to be connected "
"before proceeding, emitting warnings if the FlexiSoft driver is absent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:21
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:22
msgid "Parameters can be supplied via the launch file or CLI:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:23
msgid ""
"`topic_to_plc` (`string`, default `/flexisoft/Assem141/out_raw`) – Outbound "
"PLC assembly topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:24
msgid ""
"`topic_from_plc` (`string`, default `/flexisoft/Assem131/in_raw`) – Inbound "
"PLC assembly topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:25
msgid ""
"`assembly_size_to_plc` (`int`, default `10`) – Total byte length of the "
"outbound array; must cover every configured index."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:26
msgid ""
"`speed_index`, `direction_index`, `rotate_index` (`int`) – Byte offsets "
"(little-endian) where scaled data is written. Bounds are checked at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:27
msgid ""
"`pub_basic_index`, `sub_basic_index` (`int`) – Byte offsets that carry the "
"basic control/status bitfields described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:28
msgid ""
"`scale_drive_vector_speed`, `scale_drive_vector_direction`, "
"`scale_drive_vector_rotate` (`double`) – Unit conversions applied before "
"packing (defaults: `100.0`, `10.0`, `180.0/M_PI`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:29
msgid ""
"`watchdog_interval_ms` (`int`, default `500`) – Period for toggling "
"`watchdog_request_from_jetson`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:31
msgid "PLC basic bit layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:32
msgid ""
"Publish byte (`PubBasicData`, defaults to watchdog response off / emergency-"
"stop asserted): `bit0` watchdog response → PLC, `bit1` watchdog request from"
" Jetson, `bit2` emergency stop request, `bit3` deactivate request, `bit4` "
"SLS OFF request, `bit5-7` reserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:33
msgid ""
"Subscribe byte (`SubBasicData`): `bit0` watchdog request from PLC, `bit1` "
"watchdog response from PLC, `bit2` emergency stop active, `bit3` power cut "
"active, `bit4` move permitted, `bit5-7` reserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:35
msgid "PLC application bit layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:36
msgid ""
"Publish byte (`PubApplicationData`): `bit0` is moving, `bit1` has error, "
"`bit2` battery low, `bit3` is collaborating, `bit4-7` reserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:37
msgid "Subscribe byte (`SubApplicationData`): all 8 bits reserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:39
msgid "Building"
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:45
msgid "Running"
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:57
msgid ""
"Ensure `/drive/std_vector2` and the FlexiSoft PLC topics are available "
"before starting; the node aborts if Pub/Sub connections are missing for 10 "
"seconds. Provide `/install/license.yaml` so the built-in `KeyCertification` "
"check can validate the runtime license."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:59
msgid "Notes / Best practices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:60
msgid ""
"Keep `assembly_size_to_plc` consistent with the FlexiSoft configuration; an "
"undersized buffer prevents the node from writing scaled vectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:61
msgid ""
"Tune the `scale_*` factors and indices to match the PLC project any time "
"FlexiSoft addresses change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:62
msgid ""
"Monitor `/triorb/error/str/add` for out-of-range speeds/angles; these "
"indicate mis-scaled commands or upstream bugs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:63
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"When testing, call `ros2 service call /srv/plc/emergency_stop/request "
"std_srvs/srv/Trigger {}` to validate the PLC reacts as expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../packages/triorb_sick_plc_wrapper/standard_docs/original/README.md:64
msgid ""
"Namespacing the node? Just set `ROS_PREFIX=myrobot` before launch to scope "
"every topic/service automatically."
msgstr ""
